You will see:

Running on http://127.0.0.1:8080


 Keep this running

 PART 3 — Create a Simple Failing GitHub Actions Workflow

(Perfect for demo — no VM)

 Create workflow folder:
cd ~/Gen-AI-DevOps
mkdir -p .github/workflows

 Create workflow file
vi .github/workflows/ai-demo.yml

 Paste this YAML:
name: AI Debugger Demo

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main
  workflow_dispatch:

jobs:
  run-demo:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v3

      - name: Intentionally create an error
        run: |
          echo "Creating a CI failure..."
          pip install invalid-package-name

Save file (ESC → :wq)
PART 4 — Trigger Pipeline
 Push the new workflow
git add .
git commit -m "Added AI demo workflow"
git push

Pipeline will run automatically

Go to:

https://github.com/youraccount/yourepo/actions

You will see:

❌ Pipeline failed (expected)

Open the failed run
Note the run_id from URL:

Example:

https://github.com/.../actions/runs/19432728138
run_id = 19432728138

PART 5 — Debug the Error Using AI Debugger

Open a new Cloud Shell tab
(Flask still running in tab 1)

 Call AI debugger manually
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/debug \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d "{\"run_id\": \"19432728138\"}"

 Expected AI response:
{
  "run_id": 19432728138,
  "status": "Error detected",
  "summary": "The pipeline failed during pip installation.",
  "log_snippet": "ERROR: Could not find a version that satisfies the requirement invalid-package-name"
}

